documentation
text

	^ 'Text model: String>>asRopedText answers a BlRopedText (subclass of BlText, see Bloc-Text-Rope). BlText offers a fluent styling API on the text instance: fontSize: 24, fontName: NSimSun, foreground: Color red, bold, italic, weight:, background:, attributes: aCollection, attribute: from: to:, and range styling via (text from: 1 to: 2) fontName: .... Render it with BlTextElement new text: aBlText, or with aBlText asElement. BlTextElement supports highlighting (highlightCategory:with:), selection and measurement strategies. IMPORTANT: the font setter is fontName:, there is no fontFamilyName:. For CJK glyphs use a font family that actually contains them AND renders reliably in this environment; on Windows the working font for this project is NSimSun (Microsoft YaHei did not render). Toplo widgets carry the font on their ToLabel: buttons need button label fontName:, text editors accept codeFontName:. BlText announces changes (when:do:) and is the data holder: never conflate the text model with its visual element.'